<title>INDIA: Indian soybean up, oil firm, meal down.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean up, oil firm, meal down.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices remained bullish in central Indian markets on good purchasing from processing plants on Friday, dealers said. Prices were up by 200-250 rupees per tonne. Business volume was good and the undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were firm and decreased by 200 rupees per tonne on limited supplies. Business volume was good and the undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices decreased on limited demand at higher price level. Soymeal yellow was $265-268 per tonne FAS (free alongside ship) at Indian west coast ports. Rapeseed extraction was $98-100 per tonne FAS (free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 3,500-3,550 rupees per tonne in FOR (free on rail) condition. Business volume was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
